  {
   "id": 23,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    0,
    2220
   ],
   "size": [
    620,
    480
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "This workflow is the reel cron job's (Airflow 'instagram_reel'): every run reads it from here. Edit it and save it (same name); the next run uses it. No Git.\n\nWhat the job takes from it: every Documentary node's settings (mood, max_seconds, words, models, voice, music, transitions, subtitles, thumbnail, post), the Documentary Prompts node (when connected to Story), the Documentary Look node (when connected: a new look each run, by the seed), your own voice (the Load Audio connected to Narrate's my_voice; the job uses your recording in Nextcloud, not the file here), and the number of photos: the Photo nodes connected to Story (now 5; delete or add some, 3 to 10). Muted or bypassed nodes don't count.\n\nWhat the job sets itself: the photos (from Immich: the queue album 'Next reel' when it has 3 or more photos, which then also sets the count; else the PHOTOGRAPHY album), target (Instagram reel), seeds. Mood 'auto (from photos)': one of the reel formats (Airflow's REEL_MOODS) at random, not the last reel's.\n\nPhoto order in the queue album: as taken; a photo whose Immich description starts with '#1', '#2', ... goes to that place.\n\nYou can also run this workflow by hand with your own photos."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "type": "DocumentaryPrompts",
   "pos": [
    -580,
