  {
   "id": 25,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -580,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    540,
    600
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "Documentary Prompts: every text the Story and Social Post nodes send to the LLMs, in the order a film uses them. Each box opens with its own explanation.\n\n1. photo_analysis: what the vision model reports about each photo (subject, activity, setting, framing). The writer knows only this.\n2. moods: the tone of each mood in Story's 'mood' dropdown (one line each).\n3. auto_mood: how mood 'auto (from photos)' picks one.\n4. reel_formats: the reel moods with a fixed job per photo (mini-documentary, photographer's craft, species spotlight) and their word limits.\n5. writing_rules: the rules in every request to the writer (don't describe what's visible, facts only from the reference, names).\n6. story_plan: the plan before writing: title, beats, opening line, thumbnail hook, closing 'follow' line, camera moves, cover photo.\n7. per_photo: extra instructions for each photo's narration.\n8. social_post: the caption, title, hashtags, tags and key phrases.\n\nHow to edit: lines starting with '#' are comments. A line starting with [tag] is used only in some films ([youtube], [instagram], [story] free moods, [format] reel formats, [lens] the writer sees camera settings, [camera] camera details can show). {n} and the like are filled in. An empty box means the built-in text, so clearing one brings back the latest default.\n\nNot connected to Story: the built-in texts."
   ]
  },
